{"change_summary":"No further fixes were applied in this stage. The ninth review approved the latest remediation as-is, so the codebase remained unchanged and this pass only records that the remaining notes were non-blocking follow-ups outside the required scope of this bead.","outstanding_risks":["Legacy process field names such as `plant_half_saturation_n_mg_total`, `aob_k_tan_mg`, and `decomposer_k_doc_mg` still read like total-mass parameters even though runtime semantics now normalize them onto concentration- or area-based units; that rename work remains deferred to downstream normalization beads.","`TankState` convenience helpers still each recompute `self.concentrations()` when called individually in sequence, so non-hot-path callers can still pay repeated net-water-volume lookups unless they reuse `ConcentrationView` explicitly.","Schema-2 save migration still assumes legacy dissolved totals were authored against gross water volume, so a hand-edited or previously pre-migrated schema-2 file could still be rescaled again on load.","The geometry-side gross-volume API rename is source-breaking for any downstream callers outside this workspace that still reference the old method names, though that is acceptable for this internal workspace change."],"steps":[{"description":"Reviewed the approved validation output from completion round 9 to determine whether any actionable fixes remained after the latest documentation and gross-volume API remediation pass.","order":0,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Confirmed that the remaining review notes were non-blocking follow-ups only and did not require additional source, test, documentation, or backlog changes for this bead.","order":1,"status":"completed"},{"description":"Apply further code or documentation fixes.","order":2,"status":"skipped"},{"description":"Recorded the approved outcome and carried forward the existing validation record because no code changed in this pass.","order":3,"status":"completed"}],"valida